# Canonical stairs, ascending toward +x: three plain steps of equal rise,
# each tread running the full depth of the cell. Two nosing/reveal detail
# passes were tried and reverted — an overhanging tread lip reads
# asymmetric, the top step having nothing overhanging it. `ramp` is the
# physics contract: a climb resolves a diagonal, not the boxes; the
# one-third rise is deliberately the auto-step threshold.
version 1
shape stairs
grid 12
states facing
ramp
box all  0 0 0  12 4 12   # bottom step
box all  4 4 0  12 8 12   # middle step
box all  8 8 0  12 12 12  # top step
